(1953203, 267897, 23394, '<td valign="top">excellent shot!  this would look good in a series, if you had one of the oven door being opened (with the same amount of motion blur), and if you had one of the dough being worked on, as well as one with the racks being pushed around.  great perspective to be shooting from.  i can''t decide if this makes me hungry to eat, or to go out and shoot ;-)</td>', 'excellent shot!  this would look good in a series, if you had one of the oven door being opened (with the same amount of motion blur), and if you had one of the dough being worked on, as well as one with the racks being pushed around.  great perspective to be shooting from.  i can''t decide if this makes me hungry to eat, or to go out and shoot ;-)', '2005-12-15 05:11:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1953218, 268848, 23394, '<td valign="top">i was looking for something to give me the feeling of ''early in the morning''--this looks more like early in the afternoon.  as a photograph, i like the composition, but think it could use a little post-processing; as is, it is a little flat and a little soft, and doesn''t really lead me anywhere.</td>', 'i was looking for something to give me the feeling of ''early in the morning''--this looks more like early in the afternoon.  as a photograph, i like the composition, but think it could use a little post-processing; as is, it is a little flat and a little soft, and doesn''t really lead me anywhere.', '2005-12-15 05:18:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1953224, 267071, 23394, '<td valign="top">i am quite sure you are getting hammered with a very low score.  don''t take it personally--everybody has to start somewhere.  if you really want to learn how to take better pictures, dpc is a great place to start.  read the suggested tutorials, ask questions, and DON''T QUIT!  it can be frustrating, but it can also be very rewarding and fun!</td>', 'i am quite sure you are getting hammered with a very low score.  don''t take it personally--everybody has to start somewhere.  if you really want to learn how to take better pictures, dpc is a great place to start.  read the suggested tutorials, ask questions, and DON''T QUIT!  it can be frustrating, but it can also be very rewarding and fun!', '2005-12-15 05:21:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1953228, 267683, 23394, '<td valign="top">not fond of the execution.  nothing about the image really screams early, early in the am to me.  maybe if you had pushed the post-processing a bit, you might have had a more interesting/engaging entry.</td>', 'not fond of the execution.  nothing about the image really screams early, early in the am to me.  maybe if you had pushed the post-processing a bit, you might have had a more interesting/engaging entry.', '2005-12-15 05:23:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1953230, 268416, 23394, '<td valign="top">i hope you get what you''re after...</td>', 'i hope you get what you''re after...', '2005-12-15 05:24:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(1953238, 266850, 23394, '<td valign="top">my first impression was ''yuck''.  turns out, that was my 2nd, 3rd, and 4th impression as well.  i can only guess what you were after with this submission.</td>', 'my first impression was ''yuck''.  turns out, that was my 2nd, 3rd, and 4th impression as well.  i can only guess what you were after with this submission.', '2005-12-15 05:26:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1953245, 268655, 23394, '<td valign="top">i''m going to guess that this is not scoring as well as you would like.  i hope you are getting some comments as to why. from my perspective, it is basically a snapshot of some food, taken dead on, with the onboard flash.  if you want to do better, spend some time in the archives, looking at the images that do well, then try to recreate those shots yourself.  you can do it, but it takes practice.  and, it takes a lot more than simply pointing your camera at something.  beyond dpc, if you want your photography to improve, you need to learn how to get your camera to tell stories with images that invite people in and make them want to stay and visit.</td>', 'i''m going to guess that this is not scoring as well as you would like.  i hope you are getting some comments as to why. from my perspective, it is basically a snapshot of some food, taken dead on, with the onboard flash.  if you want to do better, spend some time in the archives, looking at the images that do well, then try to recreate those shots yourself.  you can do it, but it takes practice.  and, it takes a lot more than simply pointing your camera at something.  beyond dpc, if you want your photography to improve, you need to learn how to get your camera to tell stories with images that invite people in and make them want to stay and visit.', '2005-12-15 05:31:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1953251, 268671, 23394, '<td valign="top">an ornament, shot badly, in the dark.  i like the colors, but, beyond that, don''t find the image that engaging.  as for the challenge, there''s nothing here that really places it.</td>', 'an ornament, shot badly, in the dark.  i like the colors, but, beyond that, don''t find the image that engaging.  as for the challenge, there''s nothing here that really places it.', '2005-12-15 05:34:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1953257, 267830, 23394, '<td valign="top">this is one of those images that leaves me shaking my head.  it''s obvious you have a decent camera, and you know your way around post-processing.  if you aren''t getting the scores you think you deserve, check out this <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=156130#1084676" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">thread</a></td>', 'this is one of those images that leaves me shaking my head.  it''s obvious you have a decent camera, and you know your way around post-processing.  if you aren''t getting the scores you think you deserve, check out this thread', '2005-12-15 05:38:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1953259, 268057, 23394, '<td valign="top">honestly, i like the idea more than i like this particular image.  this one takes too much work to reconcile.  i was/am taken by the colors, but not by the effort to tell what i''m looking at.  this does have potential, it''s just not being realized here in this image.</td>', 'honestly, i like the idea more than i like this particular image.  this one takes too much work to reconcile.  i was/am taken by the colors, but not by the effort to tell what i''m looking at.  this does have potential, it''s just not being realized here in this image.', '2005-12-15 05:40:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1953260, 268694, 23394, '<td valign="top">interesting take on the challenge.  like the colors and composition, though.</td>', 'interesting take on the challenge.  like the colors and composition, though.', '2005-12-15 05:41:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1953262, 268690, 23394, '<td valign="top">this really looks like a shot that should not have been entered, no matter how badly you wanted an update button.</td>', 'this really looks like a shot that should not have been entered, no matter how badly you wanted an update button.', '2005-12-15 05:42:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1953274, 268321, 23394, '<td valign="top">this image doesn''t work for me, either as a photograph, or for the challenge.  as a photograph, it is too polished--there are hardly any textures.  compositionally, you are looking down on the subject.  also, he is framed in such a way as not to offer any context.  imagine how this would have turned out if you had put the camera on the ground and shot up through the fire into his face.  as for the challenge, there is no context for me that this is early, early in the morning.  the way it''s lit (and with no other context), this could be 3 in the afternoon, 6 in the evening, 8 in the morning.  all the same, i''m sure those ''librodo'' eyes will keep this shot from completely tanking for you.</td>', 'this image doesn''t work for me, either as a photograph, or for the challenge.  as a photograph, it is too polished--there are hardly any textures.  compositionally, you are looking down on the subject.  also, he is framed in such a way as not to offer any context.  imagine how this would have turned out if you had put the camera on the ground and shot up through the fire into his face.  as for the challenge, there is no context for me that this is early, early in the morning.  the way it''s lit (and with no other context), this could be 3 in the afternoon, 6 in the evening, 8 in the morning.  all the same, i''m sure those ''librodo'' eyes will keep this shot from completely tanking for you.', '2005-12-15 05:48:38.000000', NULL, 1),
