(1971792, 267110, 16739, '<td valign="top">Fantasic shot Skip , This is one of the best shots I''ve seen on this site.  I wonder what''s the record for the most favorites in one day? <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-12-22 20:37:56.</i></td>', 'Fantasic shot Skip , This is one of the best shots I''ve seen on this site.  I wonder what''s the record for the most favorites in one day? ', '2005-12-22 16:56:25.000000', '2005-12-22 20:37:56.000000', 0),
(1971999, 268623, 40718, '<td valign="top">You know, it seems most of the people asking for my comments in this challenge have shots I liked.  I gave this a 7.  It looks like you had a nice score though, 5.88 is great.<br/> <br/>I thought the composition was good.  I like the motion blur of the individual.  I wondered if you could have blown out the white at the top of the box less, but that is a very minor beef.<br/> <br/>Good stuff altogether.</td>', 'You know, it seems most of the people asking for my comments in this challenge have shots I liked.  I gave this a 7.  It looks like you had a nice score though, 5.88 is great. I thought the composition was good.  I like the motion blur of the individual.  I wondered if you could have blown out the white at the top of the box less, but that is a very minor beef. Good stuff altogether.', '2005-12-22 18:39:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(1972007, 268883, 49384, '<td valign="top">Awesome picture. Despite the fact that it wasn''t taken between 4-5 blah blah blah, it was very deserving of  the ribbon.  One of my favorite shots ever on this site.<br/></td>', 'Awesome picture. Despite the fact that it wasn''t taken between 4-5 blah blah blah, it was very deserving of  the ribbon.  One of my favorite shots ever on this site.', '2005-12-22 18:44:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(1973167, 267071, 23294, '<td valign="top">Entering an image this small into a challenge is a sure way to get lowballed by a lot of voters.  It looks like you did a longer exposure of some nice lights.  The shot has some really interesting colors.  The downside of this kind of shot is it looks like almost no effort was put into it, because we don''t always know if the motion was supposed to be there or not.  Often it''s assumed that it''s not supposed to be there and it''s voted down.  One thing you really might want to do is turn of the date on your camera.  That''s something you''ll never find in "artistic" photography, and this is mostly an artistic website.  If that''s how you wanted it to come out, good work.  For the next challenge, I would really suggest using an image with one dimention at least 600 pixels long.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-12-23 01:45:51.</i></td>', 'Entering an image this small into a challenge is a sure way to get lowballed by a lot of voters.  It looks like you did a longer exposure of some nice lights.  The shot has some really interesting colors.  The downside of this kind of shot is it looks like almost no effort was put into it, because we don''t always know if the motion was supposed to be there or not.  Often it''s assumed that it''s not supposed to be there and it''s voted down.  One thing you really might want to do is turn of the date on your camera.  That''s something you''ll never find in "artistic" photography, and this is mostly an artistic website.  If that''s how you wanted it to come out, good work.  For the next challenge, I would really suggest using an image with one dimention at least 600 pixels long.', '2005-12-23 01:44:50.000000', '2005-12-23 01:45:51.000000', 0),
(1973172, 267683, 23294, '<td valign="top">few things.  You''ve got a center composition, which isn''t always bad, but here it doesn''t really work for the subject.  I guess you couldn''t find something much more interesting at that hour in the morning.  I commend you for just waking!</td>', 'few things.  You''ve got a center composition, which isn''t always bad, but here it doesn''t really work for the subject.  I guess you couldn''t find something much more interesting at that hour in the morning.  I commend you for just waking!', '2005-12-23 01:47:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(1973175, 268728, 23294, '<td valign="top">I''d like to see more of the clock, it''s almost impossible to tell what it is without the title.  The crop seems a little close as well.  Great motion shot.</td>', 'I''d like to see more of the clock, it''s almost impossible to tell what it is without the title.  The crop seems a little close as well.  Great motion shot.', '2005-12-23 01:48:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(1973180, 267236, 23294, '<td valign="top">I''d like to see a more balanced exposure.  Who''s playing the game, what about a face or something perhaps?  If that''s what that is, I honestly can''t tell, i''d like to see more light, and detail there.</td>', 'I''d like to see a more balanced exposure.  Who''s playing the game, what about a face or something perhaps?  If that''s what that is, I honestly can''t tell, i''d like to see more light, and detail there.', '2005-12-23 01:49:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(1973184, 266380, 23294, '<td valign="top">Some seperation between the subject and the wall might give a nice effect.  There seems to be either a focus, or camera motion issue here.  Try a tripod, or bracing against something while taking pictures.</td>', 'Some seperation between the subject and the wall might give a nice effect.  There seems to be either a focus, or camera motion issue here.  Try a tripod, or bracing against something while taking pictures.', '2005-12-23 01:51:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(1973188, 268416, 23294, '<td valign="top">While this was shot in the time frame, there''s nothing in the shot that suggests what time it is.  It could have just as easily been shot during the day.</td>', 'While this was shot in the time frame, there''s nothing in the shot that suggests what time it is.  It could have just as easily been shot during the day.', '2005-12-23 01:53:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(1973198, 268860, 23294, '<td valign="top">the focus could be a little more on.  The white balance seems a little warm to me.  The horizon is strange because you weren''t looking dead on at the sign, a little to the side i think.  All in all, it''s just a sign, which isn''t going to make an impact on most people.</td>', 'the focus could be a little more on.  The white balance seems a little warm to me.  The horizon is strange because you weren''t looking dead on at the sign, a little to the side i think.  All in all, it''s just a sign, which isn''t going to make an impact on most people.', '2005-12-23 01:57:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(1973208, 267723, 23294, '<td valign="top">couldn''t have made it more obvious what time it was shot at, that''s for sure!  I don''t know if a sign however is the greatest thing to pick for a shot.  The composition is pretty centered, and with not much around it lit, there''s little to give it a place... i don''t know how to say what i want to say.</td>', 'couldn''t have made it more obvious what time it was shot at, that''s for sure!  I don''t know if a sign however is the greatest thing to pick for a shot.  The composition is pretty centered, and with not much around it lit, there''s little to give it a place... i don''t know how to say what i want to say.', '2005-12-23 02:00:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(1973214, 268046, 23294, '<td valign="top">not exactly sure what it is.  Looks like something in a mixing bowl.  From the reflections in the objects it looks like a straight on flash was used, try turning it off and putting a light off centered.  I think when you do that things look nicer than with a regular flash.</td>', 'not exactly sure what it is.  Looks like something in a mixing bowl.  From the reflections in the objects it looks like a straight on flash was used, try turning it off and putting a light off centered.  I think when you do that things look nicer than with a regular flash.', '2005-12-23 02:02:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(1973220, 268655, 23294, '<td valign="top">woulda loved to see the classic cold pizza for breakfast :-)</td>', 'woulda loved to see the classic cold pizza for breakfast :-)', '2005-12-23 02:06:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(1973228, 268630, 23294, '<td valign="top">I''m guessing you were going for somebody half asleep... i''m guessing both you and the subject WERE half asleep!  I like the focus, it''s good, one thing you might want to change is the coloration.  It''s pretty orangish, and i''d like to see some more natural hues.<br/> <br/>coming back to look at this one now i see major pixilation in the eye.  Not sure why really... perhaps it was caused by the sharpening?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-01-07 11:37:08.</i></td>', 'I''m guessing you were going for somebody half asleep... i''m guessing both you and the subject WERE half asleep!  I like the focus, it''s good, one thing you might want to change is the coloration.  It''s pretty orangish, and i''d like to see some more natural hues. coming back to look at this one now i see major pixilation in the eye.  Not sure why really... perhaps it was caused by the sharpening?', '2005-12-23 02:10:52.000000', '2006-01-07 11:37:08.000000', 0),
(1973232, 269009, 23294, '<td valign="top">I think this could have done pretty well if it were bigger.  It looks like a nice shot but there isn''t enough detail in such a small image.</td>', 'I think this could have done pretty well if it were bigger.  It looks like a nice shot but there isn''t enough detail in such a small image.', '2005-12-23 02:12:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(1973234, 267686, 23294, '<td valign="top">i like the feel of this shot!  There''s a conflict within it, the peacefullness of the bushes and trees and fog, and then the harshness of the siren and bright lights.  Love the colors.</td>', 'i like the feel of this shot!  There''s a conflict within it, the peacefullness of the bushes and trees and fog, and then the harshness of the siren and bright lights.  Love the colors.', '2005-12-23 02:15:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(1973400, 268348, 49849, '<td valign="top">I''m sorry, but this doesn''t deserve 2nd place, however, a spectacular-looking photograph, maybe 3rd place would be better and the photo in 3rd place could be 2nd :) SORRY!</td>', 'I''m sorry, but this doesn''t deserve 2nd place, however, a spectacular-looking photograph, maybe 3rd place would be better and the photo in 3rd place could be 2nd :) SORRY!', '2005-12-23 07:49:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(1973402, 268712, 49849, '<td valign="top">11th? Are you kiddin me? This should be in the top! Fantastic photograph! Congratulations!</td>', '11th? Are you kiddin me? This should be in the top! Fantastic photograph! Congratulations!', '2005-12-23 07:50:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(1973406, 268490, 48292, '<td valign="top">I WAS driving when I took this shot. I really DO have to be at work at 5 AM, and I really took this at 4:42 am. Not on the way to a club to party as someone insinuated. I dont really understand where that came from , but I guess its all left to interpretation right. that might be where you life and priorities are right now. <br/> <br/>I loved the blur and the fact that you cannot make out what each of the streaks came from. I think those objects being in focus would detract away fromthe point of the shot, which was driving fast to get to work. A blur of motion. <br/> <br/>As for the shaking, my shocks are shot due to the neverending construction along I-40 and the constant hitof potholes int he road. this was one of many shots this being the least busy that fit within what I was trying to say. <br/> <br/>the dashboard WAS included in the original shot but it was brighter thant he rest of the photo, and shook too much, it was not conduscive the the rest of the photo. <br/> <br/>I had this awesome idea for a city scape picture to be done , but my kid lost the mount to my tripod and the shot couldnt be steadied....or it was too foggy, tried the shot every day till the last possible day, then itoccured to photograph what I do everyday at that time....try to make it to work ontime. <br/> <br/>thanks for the comments</td>', 'I WAS driving when I took this shot. I really DO have to be at work at 5 AM, and I really took this at 4:42 am. Not on the way to a club to party as someone insinuated. I dont really understand where that came from , but I guess its all left to interpretation right. that might be where you life and priorities are right now.  I loved the blur and the fact that you cannot make out what each of the streaks came from. I think those objects being in focus would detract away fromthe point of the shot, which was driving fast to get to work. A blur of motion.  As for the shaking, my shocks are shot due to the neverending construction along I-40 and the constant hitof potholes int he road. this was one of many shots this being the least busy that fit within what I was trying to say.  the dashboard WAS included in the original shot but it was brighter thant he rest of the photo, and shook too much, it was not conduscive the the rest of the photo.  I had this awesome idea for a city scape picture to be done , but my kid lost the mount to my tripod and the shot couldnt be steadied....or it was too foggy, tried the shot every day till the last possible day, then itoccured to photograph what I do everyday at that time....try to make it to work ontime.  thanks for the comments', '2005-12-23 07:55:16.000000', NULL, 0),
